## Shared Data Fetcher Pattern (Eliminate Double DB Calls)

Both `generateMetadata` and the page component need the same data. Without a shared fetcher, the DB is queried twice per request.

```js
// Shared fetcher — Next.js deduplicates this at build time
async function getProduct(id) {
  if (!id || !/^[a-fA-F0-9]{24}$/.test(id)) return null;
  await connectDB();
  const product = await Products.findById(id).lean();
  if (!product) return null;
  return JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(product)); // serialize ObjectIds
}

export async function generateMetadata({ params }) {
  const product = await getProduct(params.id); // ← same function
  // ...
}

export default async function Page({ params }) {
  const product = await getProduct(params.id); // ← same function, deduplicated
  // ...
}
```

---

## Parallel Data Fetching (Eliminate Waterfalls)

Sequential fetches block each other. Always use `Promise.all()` when data is independent.

```js
// ❌ Bad — sequential, slow
const post = await getPostBySlug(slug);
const related = await getRelatedPosts(slug);

// ✅ Good — parallel, fast
const [post, related] = await Promise.all([
  getPostBySlug(slug),
  getRelatedPosts(slug),
]);
```

---

## Database Connection Pattern (Serverless)

Serverless functions are stateless — never assume a connection exists. Always call `connectDB()` at the top of every fetcher, not once at module level.

```js
// ✅ Correct
async function getProduct(id) {
  await connectDB(); // safe to call multiple times — checks if already connected
  return Products.findById(id).lean();
}

// ❌ Wrong — connection may not exist when the function cold-starts
const db = connectDB(); // module-level — unreliable in serverless
```

Use `.lean()` on every Mongoose query that doesn't need document methods — it returns plain JS objects and is significantly faster.

---

## Query Projection (Only Fetch What You Need)

Never fetch full documents when you only need a subset of fields.

```js
// ❌ Fetches entire document including images, description, etc.
const products = await Products.find({}).lean();

// ✅ Only fetches _id — used for generateStaticParams
const products = await Products.find({}, "_id").lean();

// ✅ Only fetches fields needed for a listing card
const products = await Products.find({}, "name slug images baseCost type").lean();
```

