## Images

- Always use Next.js `<Image />` — never raw `<img>` tags
- Set explicit `width` and `height` on every image
- Only use `priority` on above-the-fold images (hero, first product image)
- Do not use `priority` on sidebar, related, or below-fold images
- Use `sizes` prop to prevent unnecessarily large image variants being generated

```jsx
// ✅ Correct
<Image
  src={src}
  alt={alt}
  width={800}
  height={450}
  sizes="(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 800px"
  priority // only on hero/above-fold
/>
```

Vercel charges per image transformation. Unbounded sizes with no `sizes` prop generates many variants.

---

## Middleware

Middleware runs on every matching request — it is one of the easiest sources of hidden cost.

- Scope matcher paths as narrowly as possible
- Never run middleware globally if only a few routes need it
- Avoid DB calls or external API calls inside middleware
- Prefer Edge runtime for middleware (faster, cheaper than Node.js runtime)

```js
// next.config.js matcher — scope narrowly
export const config = {
  matcher: ["/dashboard/:path*", "/account/:path*"],
};
```

