## Serverless Function Best Practices

| Do | Avoid |
|---|---|
| Keep execution under 1s | Long-running loops or transforms |
| Cache DB query results | Repeated identical queries |
| Use `.lean()` on Mongoose | Full Mongoose documents |
| Return early on invalid input | Processing before validation |
| Use Edge runtime where possible | Node.js runtime for simple logic |

---

## Common Anti-Patterns and Fixes

| Anti-Pattern | Fix |
|---|---|
| `export const dynamic = "force-dynamic"` on product/blog pages | Remove it — use `generateStaticParams` instead |
| `revalidate = 0` | Only use this for truly real-time pages |
| `revalidate = 30` on blog/product pages | Increase to `3600` or higher |
| Two DB calls per page (metadata + page component) | Extract shared fetcher function |
| Sequential `await` for independent data | Replace with `Promise.all()` |
| `priority` on all images | Only on above-fold images |
| `find({}).lean()` for slug lists | `find({}, "_id").lean()` — projection only |
| Global middleware matcher `"/:path*"` | Scope to specific protected routes only |

---

## Vercel Cost Drivers (What Actually Appears on Your Invoice)

1. **Function Invocations** — every SSR or ISR hit counts. `generateStaticParams` eliminates these.
2. **Function Duration (GB-Hours)** — how long functions run × memory. Slow DB queries inflate this.
3. **ISR Writes** — every ISR regeneration writes to Vercel's cache. Low `revalidate` values cause spikes.
4. **Image Optimizations** — each unique `src + size` combination is a billed transformation.
5. **Middleware Executions** — runs on every request matching the matcher. Scope tightly.

> Monitor the **Functions** tab in your Vercel dashboard monthly. Sort by GB-Hours descending — the top 3 routes are almost always responsible for the majority of cost.

---

## Build Optimization

- Use `turbopack` in development (`next dev --turbo`) — faster local iteration
- Avoid importing entire libraries when only one function is needed (`import { X } from "lib"` not `import lib from "lib"`)
- Remove `console.log` statements before production builds — they slow down server components
- Keep `node_modules` clean — audit with `npx depcheck`

---

## Monitoring Checklist (Run Monthly)

- [ ] Review Vercel Functions tab — sort by GB-Hours
- [ ] Identify any route with invocations > 10K — add `generateStaticParams` if applicable
- [ ] Check ISR write spikes — increase `revalidate` intervals if needed
- [ ] Audit middleware matcher scope
- [ ] Review Image Optimizations count
- [ ] Run `npx @next/bundle-analyzer` to check JS bundle size

---

## Final Rule of Thumb

> Static is free. Dynamic costs money. ISR is the middle ground.
> Default to static. Justify every dynamic route explicitly.
